---
import Legal from '@/layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
const email = site.contact.email;
---

<Legal title="Terms & conditions" description={`Terms of use for the ${site.name} website.`} lines={['Terms &', '*conditions.*']}>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of this website, operated by {site.legal.entityName}. By using the site you agree to
    them. Work we carry out for clients is governed by a separate written agreement, not by these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the website</h2>
  <p>
    You may browse and share links to this website for personal and business reference. Please don’t attempt to
    disrupt the site, access it by automated means that place an unreasonable load on it, or use it for anything
    unlawful.
  </p>

  <h2>Content and intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Unless stated otherwise, the text, design and visual identity of this website belong to {site.legal.entityName}.
    Project imagery may belong to us, our clients or third parties and is shown for portfolio purposes. Please don’t
    reproduce it without permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Sample work</h2>
  <p>
    Projects labelled “Sample project” are demonstration pieces created to illustrate our approach. They do not
    represent work commissioned by, or endorsed by, any real client.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the information on this site accurate and current, but it is provided for general information
    only and may change without notice. Nothing on the site forms an offer or contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>We are not responsible for the content or practices of external websites linked from this site.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from your use of this website. Nothing in
    these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows when they last changed.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
